.TH ALDCTL 1 "2026-11-09" "AlphaDict 1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aldctl \- build, export and inspect AlphaDict dictionaries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aldctl
.B build
.RB [ \-o
.IR out.aldict ]
.I file.txt
.RI [ file.txt ...]
.br
.B aldctl
.B export
.RB [ \-o
.IR out.txt ]
.I dict.aldict
.br
.B aldctl
.B info
.I dict.aldict
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aldctl
converts between the plain text front-end format and the binary
.B .aldict
format used by AlphaDict.  Text files are easy to edit, so a dictionary can be
maintained in a text editor and rebuilt with one command.
.PP
Several text files can be given to
.B build
and are merged into a single dictionary; the header of the first file wins.
.PP
The text format is described in
.IR /usr/share/alphadict/doc/front-end_format.txt .
A step-by-step guide to making dictionaries is in
.IR /usr/share/alphadict/doc/make_dictionary.txt .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Read the given text files and write a dictionary.
.TP
.B export
Write a dictionary back to the text format, entries in alphabetical order.
.TP
.B info
Print the header and entry count of a dictionary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " path"
Output path.  For
.B build
the default is the base name of the first input with
.IR .aldict ;
for
.B export
it is the dictionary name with
.IR .txt .
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a dictionary from a text file:
.PP
.RS 4
aldctl build \-o mydict.aldict words.txt
.RE
.PP
Merge several parts into one dictionary:
.PP
.RS 4
aldctl build \-o mydict.aldict part1.txt part2.txt part3.txt
.RE
.PP
Export a dictionary for editing, then rebuild it:
.PP
.RS 4
aldctl export \-o words.txt mydict.aldict
.br
aldctl build \-o mydict.aldict words.txt
.RE
.SH LIMITS
Words may be at most 255 bytes, phonetics 255 bytes and explanations 65535
bytes in UTF-8.  Longer words are refused; longer phonetics and explanations
are truncated at a character boundary with a warning.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/alphadict/doc/front-end_format.txt
.br
.I /usr/share/alphadict/doc/make_dictionary.txt
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR AlphaDict (1)
